   "text": "This SMILES is read from the drawing. I estimated the length of the fatty-acid chain by eye, so that part is the least certain. I counted about 13 bonds from the terminal methyl to the carbonyl, which gives a myristoyl (C14) group; it could be one carbon longer or shorter.\n\n**Lipid side chain (top left):**\n- A myristoyl chain is acylated onto the \u03b1-nitrogen of a glutamate.\n- The glutamate keeps its free \u03b1-carboxylic acid. Its \u03b3-carboxyl forms an amide to two repeats of NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O).\n- The last of these repeats ends in an amide to the Lys \u03b5-nitrogen.\n\n**Peptide, N- to C-terminus:**\n1. N-terminal acetyl cap.\n2. Penicillamine, carrying a CMe2\u2013S group.\n3. Lys, with the lipid linker on its side-chain nitrogen.\n4. Thr.\n5. 7-Methyl-Trp.\n6. Lys, with an acetylated side chain.\n7. Penicillamine. Its sulfur forms an S\u2013S bond to the first penicillamine, closing the macrocycle.\n8. Tyr, with the phenol oxygen alkylated as O\u2013CH2CH2NH2.\n9. 2-Naphthylalanine.\n10. 4-Aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid.\n11. Glu.\n12. Asn.\n13. 3-Pyridylalanine.\n14. N-Methylglycinamide at the C-terminus.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I checked the wedges and hashes at each \u03b1-carbon and the Thr \u03b2-carbon. All come out as L-amino acids, with Thr as (2S,3R). The two penicillamines are R, which is the L-configuration for that residue.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)SS%11)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCC)C(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)%11)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc5ccc(OCCN)cc5)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc5ccc6ccccc6c5)C(=O)NC7(CCOCC7)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc8cccnc8)C(=O)N(C)CC(N)=O\n\nCorrection: the second penicillamine as written above lost its sulfur, so here is the final form with the S\u2013S closure restored.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)SS%11)C(=O